exit code: 0
----- stdout -----
Say what a step does, why, and what it would change on this machine.

Reads only. Run it before `apply --step <id>` to see the same step's plan without agreeing to any of
it.

Usage: gameready explain [OPTIONS] [STEP]

Arguments:
  [STEP]
          Which step, by id. Leave it out to list them

Options:
      --json
          Print the run report as JSON instead of a rendered summary

      --state-dir <STATE_DIR>
          Write the state directory somewhere else. Used by tests to keep runs out of the invoking
          user's real journal
          
          [env: GAMEREADY_STATE_DIR=[TMP]

      --games-dir <GAMES_DIR>
          Read your own game profiles from somewhere other than `~/.config/gameready/games`
          
          [env: GAMEREADY_GAMES_DIR=[TMP]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

